  "reason": "The records collectively make the later result plausibly reconstructible. R1, R9, and especially R14 establish SPS near 1000 °C in compositionally related multicomponent alloys and connect increasing temperature with diffusion-driven densification. R11 and R13 show that mechanically alloyed, initially BCC powders can precipitate secondary phases during SPS, while R8 indicates that distributed hard phases can act as microstructural barriers. Independently, R5, R6, R7, R15, R16, and R18 establish that dense, continuous oxide or passive films impede ionic or oxygen diffusion and improve corrosion or oxidation resistance. Combining these teachings would plausibly lead an expert to SPS a ball-milled BCC HEA near 1000 °C and expect densification, oxide precipitation, hardening, and diffusion-barrier protection, although the exact AlV2O4/FeAl2O4/FeTiO3 assemblage, numerical properties, and biphasic parabolic kinetics are not specifically disclosed."
